    "hardware_api_reference": "https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v5.4/esp32s2/api-reference/network/esp_wifi.html",
    "primary_measurement": "Each CSV row represents a frame in a ranging exchange. A timestamp-anchor pair can occur on multiple rows. The physical setup was one gantry robot with fixed anchors.",
    "validity_rule": "Count four integer timestamps with all values >0 and t4>=t1 and t3>=t2. These inequalities compare only fields on the same device clock. This is a completeness/ordering test, not a certification of propagation time or clock alignment. All source rows, zero values, and nonnumerics are retained in counts.",
    "timestamp_basis": "The provider documents frames.t1 to frames.t4 in picoseconds. Outer timestamp range is reported as source integers without a time-unit conversion.",
    "rtt_unit_discrepancy": "Data card labels frames.rtt (per-frame) ns. ESP-IDF v5.4 for ESP32-S2 lists wifi_ftm_report_entry_t.rtt in ps. The source card and SDK both label report-level rtt_est and rtt_raw as ns. Raw per-frame limits remain unlabeled by design. The dataset release's exact firmware build has not been established.",
    "arithmetic_check": "On integer values compute D=(t4-t1)-(t3-t2), nominally picoseconds. Raw equality holds on 15150/15152. On circle and zigzag3 one row each has raw frames.rtt=0 and D=-7812 and -9374 ps respectively. A negative D is preserved; do not infer a physical negative duration. No timestamp correction or overwrite performed.",
    "counts": {
      "rows": 15152,
      "distinct_timestamp_anchor_pairs": 1062,
      "four_timestamp_numeric_rows": 15152,
      "four_positive_and_within_clock_order_rows": 15152,
      "frame_rtt_zero_rows": 2,
      "frame_rtt_missing_or_nonnumeric_rows": 0,
      "raw_equal_four_timestamp_difference_ps_rows": 15150,
      "negative_four_timestamp_difference_rows": 2
    },
    "aggregation": "Min and max include zeros. Missing or non-integer values are counted separately. Distinct timestamp-anchor pairs are counted within each sequence then summed. No effective independent sample size or between-robot AoI is inferred."
